ercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/99c5f65c-0122-96ab-7758-2be71e42a559.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🌊 Straight from Norfolk with </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Benchtop</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Lab Jorts </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>West Coast Pilsner<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Mega Peacharine</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA with Peacharine</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/da446ddd-5eb1-9780-a440-c31558c3f08e.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🐈</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Fat Orange Cat </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>feeling fiesty<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Chonky Cat</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> NE DIPA with Citra &amp; Mosaic<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Baby Elves </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>DIPA with Galaxy, Citra &amp; Simcoe</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/d9891ffd-3c98-00b0-aa4f-0522e279c2cd.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🐇 Stay hoppy my friends<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Fair State Double Party </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Hazy DIPA with Citra &amp; Luminosa<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Bear Chase Evenin Sunset</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Afterglow Guild Trip </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>West Coast Pilsner with Celeste</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/97174c91-622d-c617-9498-9b9d7ba5e798.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍃 Fresh hazies from </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Nepenthe</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Silent Curse</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA with Riwaka, Nectaron, Motueka &amp; Vic Secret (collab with </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Astro Lab</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>)<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Phantom Scream</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy DIPA with Citra, Mosaic Incognito &amp; Simcoe</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/41ae8cb9-0430-1d33-6759-19318516a279.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f300/72.png\" alt=\"🌀\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> Hurricane incoming</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Heavy Seas Winter Storm Category 5</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Imperial ESB</span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/8e771766-4438-a9f1-ebf8-2f5575deeb03.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🌲Holly Jolly<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Deschutes Jubelale </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Winter Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Tox Holly</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Holiday Ale<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Evil Twin Before During and After Xmas </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>IPA DIPA dry-hopped with Galaxy, Motueka &amp; Sabro.⁠<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Alewerks Family Christmas</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Spiced Ale<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> 21st Ammendment Fireside Chat </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Spiced Winter Ale</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>Final Gravity Space Force Hazy IPA</p>\n<p>Hop Butcher Green Moss Hazy DIPA</p>\n<p>Finback Roll With It West Coast IPA</p>\n<p>Bear Chase Shadow Paw Coffee Porter</p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/f13d597f-3f67-2a97-75c5-0535e84895f1.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Maison Willm Cremant d'Alsace Brut Rose</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>As a huge fan of Alsatian wine, I'm grateful for Willm founder Emile Willm who shipped Alsace’s first wines to the United States once Prohibition ended in the early 1930s. Made entirely from Pinot Noir, this Cremant Rose has lovely roundness and texture, with a delicate profile of cherry, cassis, and raspberry.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Cloisonne Pinot Noir</span></span><span><span>:</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Cloisonné crafts small batches of wine from growing areas around California, including this gorgeous Sonoma Pinot Noir. French oak adds polish and balance to the vibrant dark cherry, cola, and earthy spice.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Architect Cabernet Sauvignon</span><span>: </span></strong><span><span><span><span>Architect is a tribute to Michael Broadbent - the famous British wine critic who was a bit of a jack-of-all-trades. See Beth’s writeup, below, for all the details.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/c945aa79-3968-fb61-36f1-2a64a050de74.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>We've had a lot of fun tasting new wines as we shift our wine selection from summer sippers to warm weather cozy. The latest addition in that effort is </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Architect Cabernet Sauvignon</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> from the Broadbent family. The Architect line-up of wines is a tribute to Michael Broadbent - the famous British wine critic who also happened to be an artist, author, musician, auctioneer, and architect.<br><br>Coming from the Alexander Valley in Sonoma, Architect is primarily Cabernet Sauvignon with a dash of Petit Verdot, Cabernet Franc, Merlot and Malbec. The grapes come from a diverse range of elevations in the Alexander Valley - from 134 up to 2,200 feet - and a similarly diverse range of soil types including gravel, clay and loam. As you might expect with a name like Architect, this bottle of Cabernet Sauvignon is both precise and complex. The grapes ferment in stainless steel before aging in French oak giving the wine structure and depth to compliment the fruit. Speaking of fruit, Architect certainly isn't messing around delivering dense blackberry and raspberry paired with cassis, cedar and spice. A bottle that delivers warmth, depth and wonderful velvety tannins.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>With the leaves finally turning red, I paired Architect Cabernet with my first pot roast of the season. But it's also a good match for a burger or a Thursday that just needs a pick me up. </span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Beth</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/d9fbdb97-b413-ec30-bc34-336ee4155d1b.png\" width=\"612\" alt=\"breathe11x17in_1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
